/* --- KBDVECS / IOREC exposed to TOS programs (XBIOS 34 / 14) --------------
   LDW Power calls Kbdvbase() and then reads/writes the 5th pointer, mousevec
   (offset $10).  Without a real, writable structure the call returned 0 and the
   program read address $10 - which is what killed it before its first GEM call.
   These live in the program's own TPA memory so the guest can read and write
   them, exactly like the real system variables. */
